{"rsid":2705,"house":"Rajya Sabha","name":"Shri Khiangte Laltluangkima","reviewed_at":"2026-10-29T22:19:46.654Z","sections":{"questions":{"source":"https://rsdoc.nic.in/Question/GetMeber_Question?mpcode=2705","status":"available","total":0,"source_total":0,"records":[]},"special_mentions":{"source":"https://rsdoc.nic.in/memberGetdata/Get_SpecialMentionmemberwise?mpcode=2705","status":"available","total":1,"source_total":1,"records":[{"mp_code":2705,"mp_name":"Shri                KhiangteLaltluangkima","sr_no":83,"subject":"Concern over recent landslides and natural calamities in Mizoram","sess_no":271,"SM_Text":"<p><p class=MsoNormal style=margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:\r\n-1.0in;line-height:normal><span lang=EN-US style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Times New Roman\",serif>Shri Khiangte Laltluangkima:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style=margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;text-justify:\r\ninter-ideograph;line-height:normal><span style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Times New Roman\",serif>I seek to draw? attention of the&nbsp;Government to\r\nthe serious situation arising from repeated landslides and other rain-related\r\ndisasters across Mizoram during the current monsoon. More than 100 major\r\ncalamity incidents, including around 74 landslides, besides rockfalls, storms,\r\nland subsidence, retaining-wall collapses and mudflow, have been reported\r\nacross the State. Khawzawl alone has reported about 30 landslides. Numerous\r\nsmaller landslides have also occurred across towns and localities. These\r\nincidents have repeatedly disrupted vital road connectivity. Major landslides\r\nalong NH-54A in Lunglei stranded travellers and damaged houses, while recurring\r\nrockfalls at Ngaizel in Aizawl threaten a vital road serving southern Mizoram\r\nand two major hospitals. In Serchhip, 143 families and houses were affected,\r\nwhile a major hailstorm in Mamit affected 198 families and houses. The State\r\nGovernment, DDMAs, SDRF, PWD, BRO/BRTF, NHIDCL and local communities are\r\ncontinuously undertaking relief, evacuation and road restoration. I urge the\r\nGovernment to provide&nbsp; financial and technical assistance for permanent\r\nslope stabilisation, retaining structures, drainage, rockfall protection,\r\nearly-warning systems and adequate road-clearance machinery through SDRF/SDMF\r\nand other appropriate mechanisms. Mizoram needs a long-term landslide\r\nmitigation and resilient-infrastructure programme to protect its people and\r\nlifeline connectivity.&nbsp; </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal align=right style=margin-bottom:0in;text-align:right;\r\nline-height:normal><span style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Times New Roman\",serif;\r\ncolor:#1F1F1F>(ENDS)</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style=margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;\r\nmargin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;text-indent:\r\n-1.0in;line-height:normal><span lang=EN-US style=font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\r\n\"Times New Roman\",serif></p>","Admis_Sno":0,"Made":"y","made_Date":"12/08/2026","Ministry":"HOME AFFAIRS","dt_iss":null,"proposed_dt":null,"MIN_NO":"33","Permitted":"y","Date_Permission":"-         ","sno_made":83,"dt_final":null,"reply":"No Reply","made_date_compare":"2026-08-12T00:00:00"}]},"committees":{"source":"https://integration.rajyasabha.digital/committee-integration/api/v1/web/mp/Get_Committee_DetailMemberwise?mpcode=2705","status":"available","total":2,"source_total":2,"records":[{"memname":"Khiangte Laltluangkima","comname":"Papers Laid on the table","comm_code":7,"comm_code_old":"7","frmdate":"2024-10-22 00:00:00","date":"22/10/2024","type":"Member","house":"Rajya Sabha"},{"memname":"Khiangte Laltluangkima","comname":"Commerce","comm_code":13,"comm_code_old":"13","frmdate":"2026-09-26 00:00:00","date":"26/09/2026","type":"Member","house":"Rajya Sabha"}]},"attendance_sessions"